{%- comment -%}
  Page transitions — rendered from layout/theme.liquid, next to the preloader.

  Configured from Theme settings -> Page transitions, not a section. It belongs
  to the layout rather than to any one template, and a static section rendered
  from theme.liquid would show up in the section list of whatever page the
  merchant happened to be editing.

  Ordered after bf-preloader in the layout so the intro panel is later in the
  DOM as well as higher in z-index — on a hard load both exist for a moment and
  the intro is the one that owns the screen.

  Styles are in assets/bf-page-transition.css, pulled in from <head> where being
  render-blocking is correct: the panel is full-bleed and must already be
  clipped away on the first frame.

  NO COLOURS ARE SET HERE. The panel takes the active theme's inverted pair
  straight from the tokens on <html>, so it re-resolves the instant a visitor
  moves the theme switcher — see the header comment in the stylesheet. An inline
  --page-transition-bg from a merchant setting used to live on this element, and
  it beat every stylesheet rule by virtue of being inline.

  The script is NOT deferred behind the preloader's. It only needs to exist
  before the first click, and a visitor can click during the intro.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.page_transition_enabled -%}
  <bf-page-transition>
    <div class="page-transition" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- comment -%}
        The mask is what the letters rise out of and drop back into — same
        arrangement as the preloader's, one size down. letter_class is what lets
        the CSS and JS find the individual paths; without it they carry only
        bf-wordmark__letter and nothing moves.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="page-transition__mark-mask">
        {%- render 'bf-wordmark', class: 'page-transition__mark', letter_class: 'page-transition__letter' -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </bf-page-transition>

  <script src="{{ 'bf-page-transition.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
